# Secrets -- never commit your real key. CFBD_API_KEY is stored as a
# GitHub Actions secret instead (see README for setup steps).
.env

# Local virtual environment
.venv/
venv/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# NOTE: data/raw/, data/clean/, docs/data/, and the Excel tracker are
# intentionally NOT ignored (db/schema.sql isn't either) -- the GitHub
# Actions workflow commits them back to the repo on every run so the site
# and database stay live/current without needing a local machine running
# anything.

# The COMPILED DuckDB file itself, however, IS ignored (added once the
# drive/play full-history backfill pushed it past 175MB, over GitHub's
# hard 100MB per-file limit for a normal push). It doesn't need to be
# committed: every table in it is fully rebuilt from data/raw/ by
# build_db.py/power_rating.py/features.py on every single pipeline run --
# both here locally and in GitHub Actions, which always starts from a
# fresh checkout and reruns the whole pipeline rather than resuming from a
# persisted .duckdb file (build_db.py's own DELETE-then-INSERT pattern
# means it was already a full rebuild from data/raw/ every time, even when
# the compiled file used to be committed). If you need a local copy after
# a fresh clone, just run python src/run_pipeline.py (or src/build_db.py
# on its own, followed by src/power_rating.py + src/features.py).
db/*.duckdb
db/*.duckdb.wal
